in pre lesson we create a dynamic array from scratch!

but java develop them as "ARRAY-LIST" & "VECTOR"
both of them like our DynamicArray class use "ordinary java array" under the hood!
they have 2 difference

1. ARRAY-LIST increase 50% when he need grows
   VECTOR increase 100% when he need grows

2. VECTOR is "synchronized"
   it means just one thread can touch VECTOR obj simultaneously
   but ARRAY-LIST obj can touched by multiple thread simultaneously.

Note: ARRAY-LIST is more usual,
      because it doesn't waste memory (50%)
      because it support multi thread!

